 one-character change to the text it claims to pin scores 35/35, MEASURED</span><span class="tip">sgi_re_width_probe.py&#x27;s `other kill` row is a DEATH-ONLY oracle -- a one-character change to the text it claims to pin scores 35/35, MEASURED — witness: harness:MEASURED by the #497 pass-2 seat in its own clone, with the prediction filed BEFORE building.  base 35/35 CONTROL=OK; x_othertext (catch-all message text altered, exit(1) untouched) 35/35 with ZERO red rows; x_readtext (one read arm&#x27;s text altered) 34/35, reddening `tlb_a ld kill got=exit1-txt want=exit1+txt`.  The matched pair is the point: it proves the six siblings ARE failable and this one is not.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none">