lclass was the one CORRECT clearance: held at review, all seven named seats answered at review.  A strictly-later + same-stage test keeps all six and clears that one.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">gxprobepccache</span><span class="ttl">gxprobe cached the pc across `step`, so a driver that stepped without _exec_at() had its next pc assignment silently skipped -- a detector row that could not fail</span><span class="tip">gxprobe cached the pc across `step`, so a driver that stepped without _exec_at() had its next pc assignment silently skipped -- a detector row that could not fail — witness: harness:MEASURED by the #497-family measuring seat and re-verified here.  `gxprobe.py` skips a redundant register assignment when `cache_regs` is on; `_exec_at()` pops the cached pc after stepping, but a driver calling `send(&quot;step&quot;)` DIRECTLY did not -- so its next `set_reg(&quot;pc&quot;, a)` was dropped as redundant.  The transcript is unambiguous: the first access carries a `pc=` line, the second and third do not, and they execute `nop`.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">sgideprimop</span><span class="ttl">dev_sgi_re.c draw_primitive(): a guest-written drawing op ends the host -- 254 of 256 top-byte values reach `default: fatal(); exit(1);`</span><span class="tip">dev_sgi_re.c draw_primitive(): a guest-written drawing op ends the host -- 254 of 256 top-byte values reach `default: fatal(); exit(1);` — witness: probe:regress/artifacts/sgidewidth/opus_witness_20260831 -- MEASURED by the sgidewidth measuring seat as a 24/24 ATTRIBUTION probe on unmodified `-E sgi -e ip32`: identical instruction, identical alignment, offsets differing ONLY in bit 0x800.  At `+0x7xx` (startFlag clear) `sd`/`sw`/`lw`/`ldl`/`ldr` all leave the host ALIVE; at `+0xfxx` (startFlag set) every one gives `exit 1` with `sgi_de: UNIMPLEMENTED drawing op = 0x00000000` and ZERO width messages.  The controlled single-bit difference is what makes it attribution rather than coincidence.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — UNKNOWN — [HELD AWAITING SEAT: codex, grok, kimi, opus5, fable5]  *** THIS MARKER REPLACES FIVE `NOT-FIRED&#x27; SEAT ENTRIES I WROTE EARLIER TODAY, AND REMOVING THEM IS A CORRECTION, NOT TIDYING. ***  `check_stage_panels.py` adds a seat id to the stage&#x27;s set REGARDLESS OF OUTCOME -- only HELD-token and annotated entries are skipped -- so five entries recording that a seat was NOT fired made this stage read **9/9, a complete panel, when three seats had answered**.  The gate went GREEN on a roster I had falsified, which is the seat-failure-counted-as-agreement shape arriving through the bookkeeping rather than through a silent blank.  *The checker&#x27;s own comment predicts it: &quot;otherwise marking a gap would close it.&quot;*  **WHY THESE FIVE ARE HELD, so the marker carries its question rather than a disposition note:**  they are the FILE-READING and Agent seats, deliberately not fired while a measuring seat with time-based oracles was running -- a deferral, not a failure.  **The question they are held for:** grep the fork for an existing precedent before choosing among the six de-fatalisation members for `draw_primitive()`&#x27;s `default:` arm, and say whether FAULT has any in-tree warrant here; then give the smallest edit that breaks a latch+decline fix while still passing a detector built for it.  *Two of the three premises the packet-fed seats refused have since been settled by reading and are recorded on this row: there is NO common tail after the switch, and `op` reads the memset reset value 0 = DE_PRIM_POINT.  The third -- the complete blast radius -- is settled to one certain row and one conditional on wording.*  agy is recorded separately as deliberately not fired under the measurement reservation. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — UNKNOWN — *** RESERVED FOR MEASUREMENT by owner ruling.  NOT a seat failure and NOT agreement. *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  *** THE ROUND&#x27;S BEST FINDING AND IT LANDS AGAINST THE AUTHOR: the 2-of-4 reframing is a PARTITION of the 254/256 claim, not a correction, and recording only the sharper half is the locally-true restatement that hides the defect. ***  Also asked the one checkable caveat nobody else did -- are op bits [31:26] live? -- which on checking WIDENED the defect: the primitive field is bits [25:24] and the mask is [31:24], so a legal LINE or RECTANGLE with a stray high bit also dies.  Named four premises as not settleable from the packet, each with the single fact that would settle it, and separated the all-zeroes CONSTANT from the register&#x27;s RESET VALUE. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Supplied the clause-(d) mutant BEFORE the fix exists -- drop the `!` from the guard, so the latch never sets and the announce never fires while the bit name and the absent exit(1) both still read correct -- AND the row that kills it: two distinct unimplemented primitives in one session, expecting exactly one message.  Precision correction: 254/256 counts MASKED TOP-BYTE CLASSES, not full 32-bit op values. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Refused the no-common-tail premise and answered CONDITIONALLY ON BOTH BRANCHES, naming #498&#x27;s `goto`-to-reach-the-tail as the governing precedent if a tail exists.  Marked the uninitialised-register inference as REASONED rather than READ -- the distinction the author had blurred. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">pcc2widthkills</span><span class="ttl">dev_pcc2.c has TWELVE width kills -- twice #497&#x27;s six -- every one `if (len != 1) { fatal(); exit(1); }`, so an ordinary word read of a byte register ends the host</span><span class="tip">dev_pcc2.c has TWELVE width kills -- twice #497&#x27;s six -- every one `if (len != 1) { fatal(); exit(1); }`, so an ordinary word read of a byte register ends the host — witness: harness:ENUMERATED from the shipped source, 2026-08-31.  Twelve `if (len != N)` guards in `dev_pcc2.c`, at lines 359, 371, 394, 407, 429, 467, 477, 492, 507, 528, 543 and 563 -- **all twelve are `len != 1` and all twelve end in exit(1)**, checked by walking each guard&#x27;s following block rather than by grepping adjacency.  17 terminating calls in the file overall.  NO rung-3 witness: this is READ, not booted, and there is no mvme88k rig here.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">lcabadval</span><span class="ttl">dev_lca.c: FOUR chipset registers accept exactly ONE value each and end the host on anything else -- the #443 BADVAL class, guest-written values compared to magic constants</span><span class="tip">dev_lca.c: FOUR chipset registers accept exactly ONE value each and end the host on anything else -- the #443 BADVAL class, guest-written values compared to magic constants — witness: harness:ENUMERATED from the shipped source, 2026-08-31.  Eleven live terminating calls.  The value guards, each ending in exit(1): `idata &amp; ~1` (:206), `idata &amp; ~IOC_TB_ENA_TEN` (:226), `idata != 0ULL &amp;&amp; idata != 0x300800000ULL` (:241), `idata != 0x700000ULL` (:256), `idata != 0x240000000ULL` (:280), `idata != 0x3ff00000ULL` (:295).  Each diagnostic says so in its own words -- *&quot;(0x%&quot; PRIx64&quot;) from the only implemented value&quot;*.  Plus two range guards that also kill: `dev &gt;= 21` (:129) and `ofs &gt; len` (:163).  NO rung-3 witness: READ, not booted.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="divider"><th colspan="10">closed</th></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">d1</span><span class="ttl">d1  Make drive_guest.py use $LOGDIR, not the fixed /tmp/gxregress path</span><span class="tip">d1  Make drive_guest.py use $LOGDIR, not the fixed /tmp/gxregress path — commits: f92e5a1 7cfa466 0ad64b5 — Closed on the adjudicator&#x27;s finding that it was already complete. Its own PASS-WITH-GAPS regress verdict was reached by RUNNING the evidence, not reading it, and every gap it named is filed as a row. — witness: harness:the mutation census and the R1 export/hardcode kills, each re-killed BY HAND by the flagship seat (export deleted -&gt; no FAIL; driver re-hardcoded -&gt; no FAIL), gate 2 PASS 131 twice</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — CONFIRMED — It found that the item was never executed. It made it a hard prerequisite of all mutation runs. — evidence: _scratchpad/adjudication_r420_fable.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — CONFIRMED — REAL - and the planned fix would be INERT: LOGDIR is never exported by any regress script, so os.environ.get in the driver reads nothing and keeps the hardcoded path. BOTH an export (or an argv pass at gate_crossfamily.sh:42) AND the driver change are needed. The gate&#x27;s own shell redirection does honor LOGDIR, which is what hides this. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/_dispatches/opus_batchA_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — REAL — the driver hardcodes the shared log directory and the caller does not explicitly propagate LOGDIR — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/codex_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — REAL — drive_guest.py hardcodes /tmp/gxregress in drive() and ignores LOGDIR from the environment. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/agy_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — REAL — `drive_guest.py` hardcodes `/tmp/gxregress` and `lib.sh` does not export `LOGDIR` — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/grok_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — REAL — drive_guest.py:197-199 hardcodes /tmp/gxregress; LOGDIR never read; gate_hygiene grades $LOGDIR/drive_*.log — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/kimi_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — REAL — but honoring $LOGDIR alone is insufficient without a caller change too — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/glm_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — UNKNOWN — UNKNOWN — cannot read file:line; hardcoded /tmp/gxregress is plausible but unverified. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/deepseek_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — REAL — a configurable log path that the script silently ignores is a test-isolation bug. (packet-only resend after the mixed-brief stall; P3 resolved) — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/minimax_resend_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export at lib.sh:24 + os.environ.get at :197-199, ONE carrier shared by producer and grader. Rejects argv (a SECOND carrier - writer and grader could diverge) and a call-site prefix (the census must then remember it, and forgetting is silently inert - the defect class under repair). DETECTOR TRAP NAMED: do NOT use `env LOGDIR=...`, which exports from outside and stays green with lib.sh&#x27;s export missing - that tests half the defect. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/_dispatches/fable5_r1_n5_n6_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — CONFIRMED — export at lib.sh:24 AND `os.environ.get(&quot;LOGDIR&quot;) or &quot;/tmp/gxregress&quot;` at :197 - MEASURED, the or-form is REQUIRED: the .get(default) form that the other eight seats proposed writes to the FILESYSTEM ROOT when LOGDIR is empty. Also measured: the driver-only fix is CONDITIONALLY inert (dead for `LOGDIR=x; ./run.sh`, live for an exported value) - worse than uniform. A GATE-5 ROW IS MEASURED VACUOUS (in the default battery LOGDIR equals the hardcoded literal); the detector must be an offline selftest with a private LOGDIR and a synthetic rig name, asserting the FILES not the driver&#x27;s LOG= line (a half-fix kept LOG= correct while the raw log escaped). — evidence: pipeline/evidence/_dispatches/opus_r1_research_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export LOGDIR from lib.sh and derive both driver log paths from it. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/codex_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export LOGDIR in lib.sh; driver reads os.environ.get with the same default. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/agy_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export LOGDIR from lib.sh; the driver joins that directory for both pty logs. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/grok_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export at lib.sh:24 AND os.environ.get at :197-199, proven by a fake-emulator selftest wired into gate_offline.sh (a new selftest_logdir.py, not a gate-5 row). — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/kimi_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — packet: export at lib.sh:25 + os.environ.get at :196-199. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/glm_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — packet: export LOGDIR; driver reads it with the /tmp/gxregress default. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/deepseek_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — packet: export in lib.sh; resolve both pty paths via os.environ.get. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/minimax_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c hold"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">⏸</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — CONFIRMED — Implemented and committed as f92e5a1 with its detector. Gate 2 PASS (122 checks) including the two new rows; the detector was negative-controlled in BOTH directions - no/no FAIL on the unfixed tree before the edit, yes/yes PASS after. Awaiting the panel&#x27;s review of the actual diff. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/_closure/r1_research_closure_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-20 — CONFIRMED — CLOSED AS ALREADY-COMPLETE, and verified before closing rather than taken from the hold. Nobody proposed dropping these -- the adjudicator found them while asked what should be closed that no seat had raised, and its point stands: FINISHED WORK HAD SAT OPEN FOR FIVE DAYS.
