none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">sgirekills</span><span class="ttl">dev_sgi_re.c carries 21 live terminating calls -- 15 of them inside a DEVICE_ACCESS and 13 in DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_re) alone -- and the six READ arms are all guest-reachable</span><span class="tip">dev_sgi_re.c carries 21 live terminating calls -- 15 of them inside a DEVICE_ACCESS and 13 in DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_re) alone -- and the six READ arms are all guest-reachable — witness: probe:regress/sgi_re_width_probe.py -- the six `&lt;site&gt; ld kill` rows are rung-3 symptom demonstrations of THIS defect: a real guest `ld` on unmodified `-E sgi -e ip32`, exit1 with per-site attribution text, at all six windows.  Shipped by #497, gate-run, and re-measured on every battery.  The pass-1 26/26 read-dimension probe is committed beside them at regress/artifacts/widthkillclass/opus_p1_20260830/. — note: OPEN, and the committed artifact in `witness` is the REPRODUCTION, not the fix.  `regress/sgi_re_width_probe.py` shipped with #497 and carries SIX `ld kill` rows that assert THE HOST STILL DIES on an 8-byte access at each of the six windows -- they pin the defect, they do not repair it.  #497 de-fatalised the WIDTH guard only; the width test is evaluated FIRST, so a legal `ld` still reaches the kill.  *** THE ORDERING OBLIGATION IS ALREADY RECORDED IN #497&#x27;s ROUND BLOCK AND IS THE REASON THIS ROW MUST NOT BE CLOSED BY THE CHECKER: fixing sgirekills will turn a GREEN GATE RED BY SUCCEEDING, six rows&#x27; worth. ***  It therefore inherits the oracle-correction ordering -- re-pin the six rows FIRST, measure the committed build RED under the new expectations, THEN edit the code.  A row whose own detector must invert is exactly the case the shipped-work heuristic cannot read.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — Refuted the agy audit on ONE arm of six and upheld it on five -- the useful shape, because a blanket confirmation would have shipped TEX&#x27;s ACCEPT with the same warrant strength as the clean arms.  Its discriminator is the doctrine&#x27;s own wording (&#x27;the model already computes the CORRECT answer&#x27;) against the audit&#x27;s paraphrase (&#x27;backing state exists&#x27;), and it settled TEX by GREPPING FOR CONSUMERS rather than by arguing: re_tex feeds nothing anywhere in the file.  Also supplied the five ACCEPT obligations, the #497 ordering dependency for witness quality, and the round-trip row as coupling enforcement for sgitexindex. — evidence: _scratchpad/ (design adjudication; re_tex consumer grep re-checkable in-tree)</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">HELD</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — UNKNOWN — [HELD AWAITING SEAT: opus5, codex, grok, kimi, glm, deepseek, minimax]  The DESIGN is settled -- five arms clean ACCEPT, TEX mirrored-with-coupling, five named obligations, and an ordering dependency on `#497` for witness quality.  What is NOT settled is the one question the design itself leaves open, and it is a DESIGN question rather than a scheduling one: **mirrored TEX ships a readback that is knowingly wrong at overlapping offsets.**  **HELD RATHER THAN FIRED because a measurement is in flight** -- `#497`&#x27;s table 2 is running with wall-clock-sensitive oracles, and the carrier serialises panel seats against it.  Firing seven CPU-bound seats now risks a false FAIL in the round&#x27;s most expensive measurement to save an hour on a round that cannot start until that table finishes anyway.  **RELEASE CONDITION:** `#497`&#x27;s table completes.  Then this stage fires all seven missing seats in one panel, with the design above inlined so nobody re-derives it.  *The two entries here are NOT re-fired and do not count toward the nine -- a stage held for seven that closes with two is the seat-failure-counted-as-agreement shape.* — evidence: _scratchpad/ (design settled; panel owed before implementation)</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — 15 KB, empty .err, first firing after its quota wall cleared.  Confirmed the CORRECTED census (21 live / 13 / 6+6+1) line by line, derived all six guest addresses from the base registration, ruled all six arms ACCEPT on the ground that backing state exists, and upheld the sgi_de exclusion.  Given READING rather than MEASURING deliberately: it builds and measures, but a concurrent build would have corrupted the opus5 seat&#x27;s wall-clock oracles. — evidence: regress/artifacts/sgirekills/audit_20260830/</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span 