d></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">sgitexindex</span><span class="ttl">dev_sgi_re.c&#x27;s CRIME_RE_TEX index uses &gt;&gt; 3 where its three sibling arms use &gt;&gt; 1 -- consecutive writes overlap by three entries and 81 of 112 are unreachable</span><span class="tip">dev_sgi_re.c&#x27;s CRIME_RE_TEX index uses &gt;&gt; 3 where its three sibling arms use &gt;&gt; 1 -- consecutive writes overlap by three entries and 81 of 112 are unreachable — witness: harness:ENUMERATED against the shipped source, 2026-08-30.  Walked every 8-byte access in [0x1600,0x16e0): shipped base indices run 0..27, reaching 31 of 112 cells, leaving 81 unreachable, with a 3-entry overlap between consecutive accesses.  Both figures in the row reproduce EXACTLY.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">sgimtewidth</span><span class="ttl">sgi_mte serves EVERY access width and a one-byte store silently ZEROES the adjacent register -- and the obvious fix for its dead arm would CREATE a width kill</span><span class="tip">sgi_mte serves EVERY access width and a one-byte store silently ZEROES the adjacent register -- and the obvious fix for its dead arm would CREATE a width kill — witness: harness:READ and ENUMERATED against the shipped source, 2026-08-30.  The handler is `if (len == 4) ... else if (len != 4) ... else { fatal(); exit(1); }` -- the final else is UNREACHABLE.  Bounds enumerated separately: `relative_addr &amp;= ~CRIME_DE_START` (0x800) caps regnr at 511 against `mte_reg[1024]`, so there is NO out-of-bounds access.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th