14382: >
14383: > **MOST OF THE 309 ARE NOT DEFECTS AND SAYING SO IS THE POINT** — an 8- or 16-bit register loses
14384: > nothing through `(int)`. The defect needs BOTH halves: a guard testing the FULL 64-bit value
14385: > (`idata & ~MASK`, `idata != CONST`) AND a diagnostic printing the truncated one. Then a write
