598: #  zero `endswith(` in any case (measured).  Widening to processes that cannot exhibit
599: #  the defect would make this pin answer a question it is not asking.
600: #
601: #  DISCLOSED RESIDUALS, all real, none live today: `from pty import fork` with a bare
602: #  fork(); `import pty as p`; a statement-local import; `os.forkpty` directly (which is
603: #  what pty.fork wraps); `import regress.drive_guest`.  Censused at 0 apiece.  THE
604: #  PRESENT VALUE OF 2 IS CORRECT; THAT DOES NOT ESTABLISH POPULATION COMPLETENESS.
605: #
606: #  `-print0 | xargs -0` matches both neighbours: a bare xargs finds ZERO files when a
607: #  path contains a space (measured).  No space in $HERE today; the neighbours' own
608: #  comment says the three must agree, so it agrees.
609: #
610: #  NO FILENAME EXEMPTION HERE.  readiness_predicate_test.py matches neither alternative
611: #  and holds zero whole-full sites, so scoping subsumes it -- an earlier draft carried
612: #  the exemption anyway, inert and un-companioned by a content pin, which is the shape
613: #  :92-95 condemns.  opus5 found it dead and it is gone.
614: pty_driving() { find "$HERE" -name '*.py' -type f ! -path "$HERE/artifacts/*" \
615:                      -print0 2>/dev/null \
616:                 | xargs -0 grep -lE 'pty\.fork|forkpty|pty\.spawn|^[[:space:]]*(import|from) drive_guest' 2>/dev/null; }
617: pty_code() { pty_driving | tr '\n' '\0' \
